> [1]: The Helm of Brilliance should also be a light source while worn

Nah, that'd maybe overpower it. The mining helmet patch makes more
sense.

> [2]: Decapitating medusa should create a corpse and a head.

I don't think gaze attacks work when the creature is dead. They don't
work when the creature is blind...

> [3]: Trapdoors should always come out in the same place, if that's
> codeable. It makes sense. -ekiM

The hard problem is that digging a hole in the floor in one level would
create a hole in the ceiling in another (not currently loaded) level.

> [4]: Acid resistance is meaningless.  Add a couple monsters (say, a
> purple S) that spit acid for 4d10 or something

I approve of increasing the usage of certain damage types, but one
mustn't be too hasty when making monsters.

> [5]: Zapping wands of digging <: A way to make holes in the ceiling,

See 3.

> [6]: If teleporting monsters can't make it to the upstair, they
> teleport to the downstair. If they can't make it there, they teleport a
> long way from you to heal up.

I agree with a re-tooling of the tactics and strategy routines.

